    "created_at": "2022-09-13T08:39:00Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-09-13T08:39:00Z",
    "body": "Having site-supplied declarations that affect parsing would cause parsing actions at a distance that would be hard to connect in a sensible way to all entry points to parsing. (It seems unlikely that a `meta` would travel into fragment parsing invocations, for example.)\r\n\r\nMoreover, a new solution introduced now would only work prospectively when we come across this problem the next time in the future. It wouldn't solve the issue at hand relative to implementations of the current parsing algorithm already out there.\r\n\r\nHowever, if a site is willing to take extra steps to accommodate already-deployed implementations, we already have syntax for that: using explicit end tags, i.e. not omitting any end tags (`</p>` in particular) that the spec says are permissible to omit. This can even be automated on the server side by parsing (with an up-to-date implementation) and immediately reserializing.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
